# E12 ColorGame: sequential, fixed order, colors drawn by a static Random seeded as the oracle (D96), so the C# fixes
# the order of every line (exact trace, level (a)). Each turn, each agent looks around, says what it saw, then draws a
# new color. "order" checks how the kinds of line interleave, the other facts their contents in sequence.
cover all
fact order ^(I am|I saw|I did't see|My color is now|-{43}$)
fact look ^I am (\w+)\. I am looking around\.\.\.$
fact saw ^I saw: (.*)$
fact nothing ^I did't see anything interesting$
fact color ^My color is now (\w+)$
fact separator ^-{43}$
same order seq
same look seq
same saw seq
same nothing seq
same color seq
same separator count
# three agents act in each of the 9 turns after the setup turn
check look count == 27
check color count == 27
fact error (Exception|out of range)
optional error
check error count == 0
